Z||000003||Vader||05-13-2001||12:47 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85Josh:<BR><B>spideyfoot, that thing is nade of ceramic and hardened steel! You are going to need a carbide drill bit to do this. Try looking at glass drilling bits at your hardware store, or call an industrial supply house. Good luck.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It isn't really that difficult.  I used to supply the base cores for AC Spark Plug, and they are only neutral heat treated.  The material is nothing exotic either, so "conventional" tools will get the job done.<P>That's how I get them out when they are like this:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://homestead.juno.com/jlstrey/files/ACsparkplug.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>"<I>Make Me Bad</I>"<p>[This message has been edited by Vader (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
